---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber off
    actor Admin
    participant Page as Admin sites page<br/>/admin/sites
    participant Actions as Server actions<br/>utils/supabase/queries.ts
    participant DB as Supabase<br/>PostgreSQL
    participant S3 as AWS S3

    Note over Admin,S3: Covers US 2.0.4. No delete exists in the code. All steps are Proposed.<br/>Decision: delete all Site-owned data and files. Preserve user Profiles and the shared KML source.

    Admin->>Page: Select "Delete Site"
    activate Page
    Page->>Actions: getSiteDeleteImpact(siteId)
    activate Actions
    Actions->>Actions: Check session and Admin role on server
    Actions->>DB: Count the Site's SIRs, answers, attachments, homepage images,<br/>GPX tracks, Site fields, point records, safety and priority rows
    activate DB
    DB-->>Actions: Counts
    deactivate DB
    Actions-->>Page: Counts
    deactivate Actions
    Page-->>Admin: Ask to confirm. Name the number of affected records (AT1, AT2)

    alt Admin cancels
        Admin->>Page: Select Cancel
        Page-->>Admin: Close the dialog. Nothing changes.
    else Admin confirms
        Admin->>Page: Select Confirm
        Page->>Actions: deleteSite(siteId)
        activate Actions
        Actions->>Actions: Check session and Admin role on server
        alt Caller is not an Admin
            Actions-->>Page: Refuse (403), nothing deleted
            Page-->>Admin: Show the error
        else Caller is an Admin
            Actions->>DB: Begin one transaction. Delete Site page fields, safety, priority,<br/>activity-point rows, GPX rows, homepage-image rows, attachments,<br/>SIR answers and SIRs, then delete W26_sites-pa (AT3).
            alt Any step fails (AT4)
                DB-->>Actions: Error. Roll back all steps.
                Actions-->>Page: Deletion rejected
                Page-->>Admin: Show the error. The Site and all records are unchanged.
            else All steps done
                DB-->>Actions: Commit
                Actions->>S3: Delete the removed images and GPX files
                S3-->>Actions: Done or error
                Note right of Actions: S3 is outside the database transaction.<br/>A failed object deletion is logged for retry.<br/>It does not restore deleted database rows.
                Actions-->>Page: Site deleted
                Page-->>Admin: Remove the Site from the list
            end
        end
        deactivate Actions
    end
    deactivate Page

    Note over Admin,S3: In the local schema copy, W26_form_responses.site_id is ON DELETE RESTRICT, so deleteSite must perform<br/>the ordered transaction above. Profile SIR counts come from W26_form_responses and therefore follow the cascade.
